  "code": "1358",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<h2 class=\"mb-xs mt-5 text-base font-[500] first:mt-0 dark:font-[475]\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Reference Range</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Negative:</strong>&nbsp;Normal, no abnormal sugars in urine.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Positive:</strong>&nbsp;Abnormal; suggestive of glycosuria or presence of other reducing sugars.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 class=\"mb-xs mt-5 text-base font-[500] first:mt-0 dark:font-[475]\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Interpretation</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Positive results</strong>&nbsp;may indicate:</span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Glucosuria:</strong>&nbsp;Commonly due to diabetes mellitus.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Galactosuria:</strong>&nbsp;Seen in galactosemia or infant metabolic disorders.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Other reducing sugars:</strong>&nbsp;Rare metabolic conditions.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Positive reducing substances in infants warrant urgent further evaluation for metabolic disorders.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Negative result does not completely rule out small amounts of sugars or non-reducing sugars (e.g., sucrose).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Correlate with blood glucose or further biochemical tests for confirmation</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
